{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789912350,"nonce":"sASriYTlKmHbvTVZSP8VlCmNQQ0=","message":"Two fixes in da0ae2a8a117635b2e2ef7d50e1e7a6b5184c377. (1) tick's inner 'for (k in kids)' loop was cold forever: its only sites are list iterate/iteratorValue, which the interpreter serves inline without filling a cache, so cold_loop_headers saw kinds all 0 and llvm_tick waited for 16x the queue count; tick and run never reached LLVM. Those sites are now no evidence of coldness. (2) e.step/e.children alternate Prop and Mover every element, but the single-entry cache flaps to the newest class, so the top tier inlined one class behind a guard, deopted on the first iteration of the other, and recompiled with every speculation off: 1.34M generic wren_call dispatches per run. A cache entry now carries IC_POLYMORPHIC once a second class is seen (store_seen), the inliner skips such a site, and the class-hierarchy chain takes it (Mover.step inlined, Prop.step/children through their jit slots). Generic dispatches 1.34M -\u003e 58k, no deopt. NUC idle A/B vs f610b68: dyn_dispatch 0.186 -\u003e 0.114 s; delta_blue 0.085 -\u003e 0.082; method_call, ash/binary_trees, nbody, closure_call unchanged. Left: the two nocheck/slot calls per element and the GC's ~10%.","files":null}]}